---
const defaultStage = "retrieval";

const stages = [
  {
    id: "observation",
    index: "01",
    label: "Registered observation",
    center: 470,
    role: "input",
    description:
      "Top-view stereo is converted into an RGB image and a registered metric-depth map; both preserve the same image-plane coordinates.",
    regions: [{ x: 28, y: 106, width: 885, height: 958, radius: 26 }],
  },
  {
    id: "dual",
    index: "02",
    label: "Dual patch fields",
    center: 1441,
    role: "dual",
    description:
      "Frozen DINOv3 and DeFM produce semantic and geometric patch fields on a shared Hₚ × Wₚ lattice.",
    regions: [{ x: 910, y: 107, width: 1062, height: 959, radius: 26 }],
  },
  {
    id: "retrieval",
    index: "03",
    label: "RGB-indexed retrieval",
    center: 2716,
    role: "retrieval",
    description:
      "RGB patches form the queries; the compatible depth field supplies keys and values. A learned 2-D bias retains image-space structure over two retrieval layers.",
    regions: [{ x: 2034, y: 94, width: 1364, height: 956, radius: 26 }],
  },
  {
    id: "tokens",
    index: "04",
    label: "StereoPatch tokens",
    center: 3637,
    role: "tokens",
    description:
      "Only the updated RGB-indexed field R² is exposed to the policy, carrying semantic identity plus retrieved metric geometry.",
    regions: [{ x: 3410, y: 440, width: 454, height: 340, radius: 22 }],
  },
  {
    id: "policy",
    index: "05",
    label: "Policy interface",
    center: 2113,
    role: "policy",
    description:
      "The same observation tokens condition either StereoPatch-ACT’s transformer decoder or StereoPatch-DP’s denoising network; both output an action chunk.",
    regions: [
      { x: 28, y: 1182, width: 698, height: 535, radius: 26 },
      { x: 1120, y: 1182, width: 1987, height: 535, radius: 26 },
      { x: 3238, y: 1228, width: 630, height: 380, radius: 22 },
    ],
  },
];
---

<section class="section method-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading-wide">
    <p class="kicker">01 · Representation interface</p>
    <h2 id="method-title">Resolve RGB–depth association <em>before</em> policy decoding.</h2>
    <p>
      The policy receives one RGB-indexed field enriched with metric evidence—not two
      unbound token sets that scarce demonstrations must associate while learning control.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="paper-method-figure" data-method-inspector data-reveal>
    <div
      class="method-figure-scroll"
      tabindex="0"
      role="region"
      aria-label="StereoPatch method figure; use the stage controls below to inspect modules, or scroll horizontally on a narrow screen"
    >
      <div class="method-figure-stage" data-method-stage data-active-method={defaultStage}>
        <img
          src="media/method/stereopatch-method-transparent.png"
          alt="StereoPatch token construction from registered RGB and depth, followed by StereoPatch-ACT and StereoPatch-DP policy interfaces"
          width="3874"
          height="1728"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />

        <svg
          class="method-focus-layer"
          viewBox="0 0 3874 1728"
          preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false"
        >
          <defs>
            {
              stages.map((stage) => (
                <mask
                  id={`method-mask-${stage.id}`}
                  maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
                  x="0"
                  y="0"
                  width="3874"
                  height="1728"
                >
                  <rect x="0" y="0" width="3874" height="1728" fill="white" />
                  {stage.regions.map((region) => (
                    <rect
                      x={region.x}
                      y={region.y}
                      width={region.width}
                      height={region.height}
                      rx={region.radius}
                      fill="black"
                    />
                  ))}
                </mask>
              ))
            }
          </defs>

          {
            stages.map((stage) => (
              <g
                class:list={[
                  "method-focus",
                  `method-focus-${stage.role}`,
                  stage.id === defaultStage && "is-active",
                ]}
                data-method-focus={stage.id}
              >
                <rect
                  class="method-focus-dim"
                  x="0"
                  y="0"
                  width="3874"
                  height="1728"
                  mask={`url(#method-mask-${stage.id})`}
                />
                {stage.regions.map((region) => (
                  <rect
                    class="method-focus-outline"
                    x={region.x}
                    y={region.y}
                    width={region.width}
                    height={region.height}
                    rx={region.radius}
                    vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
                  />
                ))}
              </g>
            ))
          }
        </svg>

        <div class="method-hotspots" aria-label="Clickable modules in the StereoPatch method figure">
          {
            stages.flatMap((methodStage) =>
              methodStage.regions.map((region, regionIndex) => (
                <button
                  class:list={["method-hotspot", methodStage.id === defaultStage && "is-active"]}
                  type="button"
                  data-method-hotspot={methodStage.id}
                  aria-label={`Inspect ${methodStage.label}${methodStage.regions.length > 1 ? `, region ${regionIndex + 1}` : ""}`}
                  aria-controls={`method-panel-${methodStage.id}`}
                  aria-pressed={methodStage.id === defaultStage ? "true" : "false"}
                  style={`left:${(region.x / 3874) * 100}%;top:${(region.y / 1728) * 100}%;width:${(region.width / 3874) * 100}%;height:${(region.height / 1728) * 100}%;`}
                >
                  <span aria-hidden="true">{methodStage.index}</span>
                </button>
              )),
            )
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="method-inspector">
      <div class="method-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="StereoPatch method stages">
        {
          stages.map((stage) => (
            <button
              class:list={["method-tab", stage.id === defaultStage && "is-active"]}
              id={`method-tab-${stage.id}`}
              type="button"
              role="tab"
              aria-selected={stage.id === defaultStage ? "true" : "false"}
              aria-controls={`method-panel-${stage.id}`}
              tabindex={stage.id === defaultStage ? 0 : -1}
              data-method-tab={stage.id}
              data-method-center={stage.center}
            >
              <span class="method-tab-index" aria-hidden="true">{stage.index}</span>
              <span class="method-tab-label">{stage.label}</span>
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="method-panels" aria-live="polite">
        {
          stages.map((stage) => (
            <section
              class="method-panel"
              id={`method-panel-${stage.id}`}
              role="tabpanel"
              aria-labelledby={`method-tab-${stage.id}`}
              tabindex="0"
              data-method-panel={stage.id}
              hidden={stage.id !== defaultStage}
            >
              <p class="method-panel-index">Stage {stage.index}</p>
              <h3>{stage.label}</h3>
              <p>{stage.description}</p>
            </section>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    <figcaption>
      The exact Method figure used in the paper: select a module directly in the figure—or use the stage rail—to trace how registered geometry enters RGB patch addresses before either policy head decodes actions.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p class="method-boundary">
    <strong>What patch-aligned means.</strong> A calibrated stereo camera yields top-view RGB and registered metric depth. The streams share a lattice and explicit offset structure;
    StereoPatch does not assume one-to-one token matching or a fixed grid resolution.
  </p>
</section>
